{"chunk_id": "a2b70ac6d26e", "text": "Book 8 of the Mahabharata (Karna\u2011parva) opens after the death of Drona, when the Kaurava camp is shaken by grief and fear. Duryodhana appoints Karna as the new commander, hoping his prowess will turn the tide against the Pandavas. Karna leads a devastating assault for two days, slaughtering many warriors, yet the long\u2011awaited duel with Arjuna ends in Karna\u2019s death. The narrative then shifts to Hastinapura, where Sanjaya reports the catastrophe to the blind king Dhritarashtra. Overwhelmed, the king laments the fall of his greatest champions\u2014Bhishma, Drona, Karna, and many princes\u2014recognizing too late that his earlier choices and rejected counsel led to the ruin of his dynasty. The chapter emphasizes fate, regret, and the tragic consequences of pride and war.\nAfter Drona\u2019s death Karna becomes Kaurava commander, wreaks havoc for two days, and is finally slain by Arjuna, plunging Dhritarashtra\u2019s court into grief.\nThemes: fate and destiny, war leadership, grief and regret, heroic combat, consequences of past actions", "vector": [-0.0034615909680724144, -0.011806262657046318, -0.007982718758285046, 0.00752205029129982, -0.0012643691152334213, 0.035879455506801605, -0.020532630383968353, -0.0037741870619356632, -0.03279956057667732, -0.006409866269677877, 0.01416225079447031, 0.0262580756098032, -0.0012857572874054313, 0.015912789851427078, -0.00554446829482913, 0.004215112421661615, 0.03951215371489525, -0.010812535881996155, 0.019979828968644142, -0.037853747606277466, -0.0047218468971550465, -0.004856756888329983, -0.006271665915846825, 0.026034323498606682, -0.011589090339839458, 0.02798229083418846, 0.009713513776659966, -0.026021160185337067, 0.01887422613799572, -0.021480290219187737, -0.013925335370004177, -0.010950736701488495, -7.29048260836862e-05, -0.014043793082237244, -0.02424429915845394, 0.020006153732538223, -0.015254692174494267, -0.019756076857447624, 0.005995265208184719, 0.00162